  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Fritz Park is one of DFW's oldest courses — an Irving original from 1984 with Delaware Creek running OB through the layout and a pecan orchard giving the front nine its character. From the standard pins it plays 6,580 feet at par 58.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach 2 baskets, it's notable for being roughly 95% handicap friendly — an old course with surprisingly good accessibility. The creek is the real hazard: it shows up exactly when you've forgotten about it.",
    "A historic, characterful round that's been teaching DFW players for four decades."
  ],
