  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 14 is the longest at Fritz at 701 feet — a par 4 where Delaware Creek makes its biggest appearance, crossing the fairway at exactly the wrong spot. Three clean shots, or a swim. It's the hole that's been defining rounds at Fritz since 1984.",
  "localTips": "The creek is the real course hazard — it cuts through the layout and punishes the careless. Roughly 95% handicap friendly, which is rare for a course this old. Free to play with real DFW history.",
